# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# examples/basic-app — environment setup
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (Next.js auto-loads `.env.local` and it is
# gitignored) and fill in your sandbox credentials. Nothing here is prefixed
# with `NEXT_PUBLIC_`, so none of these values can ever be inlined into the
# client bundle. Use `SANDBOX` credentials — never a live API key.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Daya Business API key. Use a SANDBOX key (`sk_sandbox_...`):
#   https://dashboard.daya.co/developers/keys
# The SDK infers the environment from the key prefix (`sk_live_` -> production,
# anything else -> sandbox). Prefer leaving DAYA_ENVIRONMENT unset and rely on
# the key prefix.
DAYA_API_KEY=sk_sandbox_xxxx

# Webhook signing secret used to verify `x-daya-signature` on webhook requests:
#   https://dashboard.daya.co/developers/webhooks
# Used by app/api/daya/webhook/route.ts.
DAYA_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_xxxx

# Optional: force the environment instead of inferring it from the key prefix.
# DAYA_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox

# Optional: override the API base URL (e.g. a custom proxy).
# DAYA_BASE_URL=https://api.sandbox.daya.co